{{/*
Local chezmoi configuration, rendered once by `chezmoi init` and written to
~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml on each host.

That rendered file is never committed anywhere. It is the entire mechanism by
which one public repo produces a different result per host and per user: the
repo holds the logic, this file holds the answers.

Everything prompted for below is machine identity or personal identity, neither
of which belongs in a public repo. Note what is NOT asked: nothing about a
private layer, because this repo has no knowledge of one.

Re-running `chezmoi init` keeps existing answers — promptStringOnce only asks
for values that are not already set. To change an answer later, edit
~/.config/chezmoi/chezmoi.toml directly, or `chezmoi init --force` to be
re-prompted for everything.

The prompt strings below are kept SHORT AND STABLE on purpose. `--promptString`
matches on the prompt text, not on the variable name, so these double as the
non-interactive API used by CI:

    chezmoi init --promptString 'host slug=angler,git name=x,git email=y@z'

Changing a prompt string is therefore a breaking change to that interface.
Beware: when a prompt goes unanswered non-interactively, chezmoi substitutes the
prompt text itself as the value rather than failing, so a typo yields a config
containing "host slug" instead of an error. CI must assert on rendered output,
not merely on a zero exit code.
*/}}
{{- $hostID   := promptStringOnce . "hostID"   "host slug" -}}
{{- $gitName  := promptStringOnce . "gitName"  "git name" -}}
{{- $gitEmail := promptStringOnce . "gitEmail" "git email" -}}

{{/*
Pin the source directory to wherever `chezmoi init --source=...` was run.

chezmoi does NOT persist --source on its own: without this line the generated
config has no sourceDir and every later command silently falls back to
~/.local/share/chezmoi, leaving two clones of the repo to drift apart.

`| dir` strips the .chezmoiroot component, so this records the repository root
and chezmoi re-applies .chezmoiroot itself. Moving the repo means re-running
`chezmoi init --source=<new path>`.
*/}}
sourceDir = {{ .chezmoi.sourceDir | dir | quote }}

[data]
hostID = {{ $hostID | quote }}
gitName = {{ $gitName | quote }}
gitEmail = {{ $gitEmail | quote }}
